ARM-DOS licensing
=================

The MIT License below covers ARM-DOS's own code and documentation: the BIOS, the
DOS kernel, COMMAND.COM, the SDK, the utilities and programs written for ARM-DOS,
the JavaScript emulator, the web page and the build tools.

Third-party components keep their own licences. They are listed, with their
sources and licence texts, in disk/c/CREDITS.TXT (C:\CREDITS.TXT on the emulated
machine) and in the licence files in each component's directory (for example
apps/doom/src/LICENSE, apps/quake/src/COPYING, apps/gem/orig/aes/license.txt).
Third-party data that is not part of this repository (shareware game data,
freeware programs, music) is downloaded by tools/fetch-3rdparty.sh; its sources
and licences are listed in 3rdparty/manifest.json. Programs built from GPL-licensed
sources (for example DOOM.EXE, QUAKE.EXE, WOLF3D.EXE, KEEN.EXE, the GEM desktop)
are distributed under the GPL, and their complete source code is in this
repository.

Portions of ARM-DOS are derived from Microsoft's MS-DOS 4.00 and GW-BASIC source
code releases (https://github.com/microsoft/MS-DOS,
https://github.com/microsoft/GW-BASIC), which are available under the MIT License:

